# E §3.1 step 1 / L §6.1: `use a = "file" sha256 "..."` names the member's file; it is found relative to the joint model's
# file (members/ana.tally beside joint.tally). With pin=bytes the pin matches, and a.rate reads ana's rate (0.12).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "members/ana.tally" sha256 "caf5f7622e7fa75fe10974cb18199597c91e70a92e887654d54870c36f543c67"

ask r: a.rate
=== members/ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== expect
r: 0.12
  cut 2026-10-20
